(SENTINEL FAMILY SHIELD - POLICY WORDING) Tj T*
(UIN: SENHLIP24001V012324 | Version 1.2 | Effective April 1, 2024) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION A - DEFINITIONS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A.1 "Hospital" means an institution registered with local authorities having at least 10 in-) Tj T*
(patient beds \(15 in towns with population above 10 lakh\), qualified nursing staff round the) Tj T*
(clock, a qualified medical practitioner in charge round the clock, and a fully equipped) Tj T*
(operation theatre.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A.2 "Pre-existing Disease" means any condition, ailment, injury or disease that is diagnosed by) Tj T*
(a physician within 48 months prior to the effective date of the policy, or for which medical) Tj T*
(advice or treatment was recommended by or received from a physician within 48 months prior to) Tj T*
(the effective date.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A.3 "Co-payment" means a cost-sharing requirement under which the policyholder bears a) Tj T*
(specified percentage of the admissible claim amount. A co-payment does not reduce the sum) Tj T*
(insured.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A.4 "Grace Period" means the specified period of time immediately following the premium due) Tj T*
(date during which a payment can be made to renew or continue the policy without loss of) Tj T*
(continuity benefits. Grace period is 30 days for annual, half-yearly and quarterly modes and 15) Tj T*
(days for monthly mode.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A.5 "Day Care Treatment" means medical treatment or surgical procedure undertaken under general) Tj T*
(or local anaesthesia in a hospital or day care centre in less than 24 hours because of) Tj T*
(technological advancement.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION B - COVERAGE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(B.1 In-patient Hospitalisation: reasonable and customary charges for room, boarding, nursing,) Tj T*
(ICU, surgeon, anaesthetist, consultants, operation theatre, medicines, diagnostics, and) Tj T*
(implants, for hospitalisation of at least 24 consecutive hours.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(B.2 Pre-hospitalisation medical expenses incurred up to 60 days before admission and Post-) Tj T*
(hospitalisation expenses up to 90 days after discharge, related to the same illness.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(B.3 Day Care Treatment: all day care procedures are covered.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(B.4 Road Ambulance: up to Rs 3,000 per hospitalisation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(B.5 AYUSH Treatment: in-patient treatment under Ayurveda, Yoga, Unani, Siddha and Homeopathy at) Tj T*
(a government hospital or an institute recognised by the government, up to the sum insured.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(B.6 Restoration of Sum Insured: if the sum insured and accrued no-claim bonus are exhausted) Tj T*
(during a policy year, 100% of the base sum insured is restored once in that year, usable only) Tj T*
(for an illness unrelated to those for which claims were already paid. Restored amount cannot be) Tj T*
(carried forward.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(B.7 No-Claim Bonus: 10% of base sum insured for every claim-free policy year, cumulative to a) Tj T*
(maximum of 50%. In a year with a claim the bonus reduces by 10%, never below zero.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(B.8 Maternity: delivery expenses including pre-natal and post-natal expenses up to Rs 50,000) Tj T*
(per delivery, maximum two deliveries during the lifetime of the policy, available after 24) Tj T*
(months of continuous coverage of both the mother and the father. Newborn is covered under this) Tj T*
(limit from birth until 90 days, and may be added as an insured member from day 91.) Tj T*
